---
import ForumSampleLayout from '../../layouts/ForumSampleLayout.astro';
---
<ForumSampleLayout title="About This Sample">
  <div class="max-w-3xl"><h1>About This Sample</h1><p class="my-6 text-stone-600">This is a clickable sample of vintageguitarforum.com for Joe's review. It shows categories, discussions, member profiles, guest posts and a possible moderation process.</p>
    <div class="forum-card space-y-7 p-6 sm:p-8">
      <section><h2>What Is Real</h2><p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">Joe Dampt is the owner of Joe's Vintage Guitars. His profile facts come from his published about page. Guide links open real pages on the shop site.</p></section>
      <section><h2>What Is Placeholder</h2><p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">Every thread, reply and moderation item is demo content, including replies attributed to Joe. Sample Member 1, Sample Member 2 and Sample Member 3 represent future members. No guest shop or builder is being represented.</p></section>
      <section><h2>How The Helper Could Work</h2><p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">Forum Helper represents an AI that answers and moderates. Its answers would be checked against Joe's published guides, with uncertain questions flagged for Joe. This sample has no live AI connection.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Try It In Your Browser</h2><p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">New threads and replies save only in this browser using localStorage. They appear as Sample Member 1 with a Demo Account badge. Other visitors cannot see them, and clearing site data removes them. The guest pitch form sends nothing.</p><a href="/forum-sample/new-thread/" class="forum-button mt-4">Try A New Thread</a></section>
      <section><h2>The Platform Comes Next</h2><p class="mt-3 text-stone-600">The real forum would run on whichever platform Joe picks. Accounts, membership approval, uploads, notifications and live moderation would be built on that platform. This preview is marked noindex and excluded from the sitemap.</p></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</ForumSampleLayout>
